How popular is fast food in your country?
Well, I think fast food has gained increasing popularity in China, especially in urban areas and the younger generations. First off, many young people don't have time to cook as they are busy, so they need to order some takeout and fast food can be a quite good choice for them since it can be delivered within just 30 minutes. Secondly, I think it's more convenient to have fast food, compared to having other types of food. For stance, when we have Chinese food, we usually need chopsticks, right? But when having hamburgers, obviously we don't need any other utensils.

How do people often respond to poor customer service?
Well, I think various age groups respond in completely distinct ways. For the older generations, they tend to make some phone calls to report the issue and express their grievances. They might not be accustomed to using certain digital approaches or have no clue about social media. But for the younger generations, I believe the first thing that comes to their minds is to gripe on social media like leaving some negative remarks on the online shops. Also, they can share their experiences on personal blogs.

What changes has the development of technology brought about in our lives?
Personally, I think technology has brought both negative and positive effects on people's live. First, I admit that the advancement of technology has enhanced social media platforms, making it simpler for people to get in touch with each other and shorten the distance among people. However, this is a double-edged sword I believe. It's much easier for people to be reached even after work during their leisure time. It's much easier for their boss to give them a call and then ask them to come back to work.

What can people gain from going to natural places?
Venturing outdoors especially in natural settings offers numerous benefits. To start with, it's fantastic for physical health. People can engage in a variety of outdoor activities such as hiking or cycling. Moreover, it's an excellent method for alleviating stress. When individuals immerse themselves in nature, they can certainly shed some anxiety and depression. You see nature has this incredible ability to rejuvenate our spirits.

How does social meida help people access information?
Well, when folks are gathering information, social media is a major player. It keep folks in the loop with real-time updates on events, news and trends, ensuring they don't miss out on the latest buzz or announcements they are into. Plus, social media offers a range of viewpoints. People can tap into information from various sources. For instance, if they are on a hunt for a specific restaurant, and really want the lowdown on it, social media can give them a broader perspective, and help them make a more informed decision.

How different is life in the countryside to life in the city?
Well, there's difinitely a stereotype about life in the countryside. People often assume that folks there might not have access to the same quality of education or healthcare and they might miss out on amenities. But here's a different perspective. Living the countryside can actually bring people closer together I mean it's not like the city which is crowded, making it easy for people to become detached. That less common in the countryside. People there tend to be more warm-hearted and have more time together and celebrate special occasions.

What factors will contribute to whether a place is good to live in or not?
A lot goes into making a place great to live in. To start with, I would say the quality of life is key. We need to ensure there is access to top health care facilities and services. Plus, having quality schools is a must. As for the second factor, it's all about the community and culture. A lively social scene and atmosphere that's welcoming and inclusive can really make people feel at home and contribute to the overall quality of the place. 

Is it good to share something on social media?
Generally, i would say it's pretty solid. It has the potential to inspire more folks to voice their options on social media and for those who are really into a specific or a particular field, if they get a chance to share their expertise they can really help out a lot of people who are eager to learn. Plus, for influencers when they drop some thoughtful insights on trending topics, events and causes, it can really boost awareness about critical issues.

Why do some people still use cash?
Well, i believe it largely a matter of generational differences. Older folks might struggle to adapt to digital payment methods, such as scanning QR codes. On the other hand, Some younger generations like teenagers offen lack self-discipline. If they use cash, it's easier for parents to control their spending, which can help them manage their budgets more effectively. 

Do you prefer to study at home or study in other places?
It really varies with where I am in life. As a kid, I'd hit the library. It's a perfect spot to keep my head in the game and find that spark of creativity, especially when I had essays to crank out. But now that I'm all grown up and have been clocking in at the office for years. I've grown to love my home office setup. It's all about the cozy, familiar vibe that just feels right.
